    "text": "We are told that:\n\n- Jordan carried **twice as many balls as Jason**.\n- Jason carried **twice as many balls as Jeffrey**.\n- Jason carried **2 balls**.\n\nLet's solve this step by step.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Determine how many balls each boy carried\n\n- Jason carried **2 balls** (given).\n- Jordan carried **twice as many as Jason**, so:\n  $$\n  \\text{Jordan} = 2 \\times \\text{Jason} = 2 \\times 2 = 4 \\text{ balls}\n  $$\n- Jeffrey carried **half as many as Jason**, so:\n  $$\n  \\text{Jeffrey} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{Jason} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 2 = 1 \\text{ ball}\n  $$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Add up the total number of balls\n\n$$\n\\text{Total balls} = \\text{Jordan} + \\text{Jason} + \\text{Jeffrey} = 4 + 2 + 1 = 7\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Final Answer:\n$$\n\\boxed{7}\n$$\n\n#### <answer>7</answer>",
